			"type": "text",
			"text": "Ellimichthys is a ray finned fish discovered in Candeias Formation of Brazil and Cocobeach Formation of Equatorial Guinea, dating back to the Early Cretaceous. Its name is a reference to another fish genus 'Ellima' and the word 'ichthys' meaning fish. They were small fishes, most growing to 9 centimeters but some individuals growing to 11 centimeters. They were a distant relative of Herrings and Anchovies."
